{"abstract":"As the development of new digital technologies is increasingly mobilised as a solution to global crises, such as in healthcare and the climate crisis, design is becoming an ever more influential actor in the legislation of answers to questions of ‘how to care’. This chapter explores the relationship between participatory design (PD) activities and care. We enquire empirically into how engagement and care are done in design practice by looking retrospectively at a PD project on welfare innovation for senior citizens in Denmark through the analytical lens of care. We draw on conceptions of care in the intersection of feminist research, science and technology studies (STS), and PD scholarships. Based on this, we develop the notion of ‘project engagement technologies’ (PET) as an analytical concept, which brings into view the role of material and technical entities that, despite their triviality, enable specific forms of engagement and care in design projects, and exclude others. We propose a view on attempts at doing ‘careful engagements’ as crafted activities and suggest PET as an empirical-ethnographic resource to critically examine conditions for engagement and care in projects and assemblages that aim to do ‘careful engagement’. We argue that since design and care are already deeply entangled in practice, and sometimes in problematic and uncareful ways, exploring relations between care and design may be an interesting topic for STS, opening new possibilities for intervention and fostering engagement and care through design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise","Poderi, Giacomo","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Karasti, Helena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798521"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"project engagement technologies and their role in shaping conditions for engagement and care in participatory design projects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-44119-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798521","identifier":[{"id":"85201998289","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0d795d6e-1fc9-48e6-871f-ffe793f42e5a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC6FBF1E4F83C60FB964634CB8E125FC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Giacomo","key":"poderipau","last":"Poderi","name":"Poderi, Giacomo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena","key":"karastipau","last":"Karasti","name":"Karasti, Helena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Doris","key":"lydahlpedh","last":"Lydahl","name":"Lydahl, Doris","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Christian","key":"mossfeldtnickelsenpedh","last":"Mossfeldt Nickelsen","name":"Mossfeldt Nickelsen, Niels Christian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-44119-6_2","eisbn":["9783031441196"],"isbn":["9783031441189"],"pages":"19-34","place":"Switzerland","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Ethical and Methodological Dilemmas in Social Science Interventions: Careful Engagements in Healthcare, Museums, Design and Beyond"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201998289"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d795d6e-1fc9-48e6-871f-ffe793f42e5a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Project Engagement Technologies and Their Role in Shaping Conditions for Engagement and Care in Participatory Design Projects","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798521","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been celebrated as a breakthrough in eldercare. Mainstream discourses emphasize voice-based technology as practical assistants, and thus figure voice as a practical means to achieve certain ends. But there is more to voice interactions than merely distributing messages and articulating commands. Voice-based interactions create sonic environments, enact affect, identities, likes and dislikes. In this presentation we will explore the phenomenon of voice-based technology in the smart-home. Through ethnographic interviews we study how older people use voice-based technologies and with what effects for their experiences of the affective environment in their homes. We combine the concept from Science and Technology Studies of infrastructure with a cultural anthropological view on voice. Based on this, we see voice-based interactions as infrastructures that link the realms of the technical, cultural and sociopolitical to the level of the individual, creating sites where shared discourses and values, affect, and aesthetics are made manifest in and contested through embodied and material practice. The presentation makes audible interactions between voices, technologies, and homes, to exemplify some of the infrastructural and affective effects of voice-based technologies. We find that the use of voice-based technologies results in changes in the affective environments of the home, such as by creating uncertainty, harshness and intervening in cultural and temporal enactments of politeness. Moreover, their ability to make voices travel beyond the material confines of the home, renders its boundaries more permeable, thus creating a sense of disempowerment both towards technology and the management of the privacy of the home. We propose the phenomenon of voice and voice-enabled technologies as an interesting topic for socio-gerontechnology research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718840"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective environment","Eldercare","Smart home infrastructure","Sonic interactions","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voice based technology and ageing infrastructures of voice environments of affect","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718840","ids":["itu-356ce93d-d91f-45e4-b870-c0945278c73f"],"keyword":["- Affective environment","- Eldercare","- Smart-home infrastructure","- Sonic interactions","- Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E24BA85805A531820E093F662B880ADE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-356ce93d-d91f-45e4-b870-c0945278c73f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voice-based Technology and Ageing : Infrastructures of Voice, Environments of Affect","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718840","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Digital voice assistants (DVA) have been celebrated as a breakthrough in eldercare. Mainstream discourses emphasize voice-based technology as practical assistants, and thus figure voice as a practical means to achieve certain ends. But there is more to voice interactions than merely distributing messages and articulating commands. Voice-based interactions create sonic-affective environments and enact cultural categories, likes and dislikes. In this paper we explore the phenomenon of DVA’s in older people’s smart homes. Through ethnographic interviews we study how older people use DVA’s and with what effects for their experiences of the sonic-affective environment in their homes. We combine the concept from Science and Technology Studies of infrastructure with a cultural anthropological view on voice. Based on this, we see voice-based interactions as infrastructures that link the realms of the technical, cultural and sociopolitical to the level of the individual, creating sites where shared discourses and values, affect, and aesthetics are made manifest in and contested through embodied and material practice. The paper analyzes interactions between voices, technologies, and homes, to exemplify some of the infrastructural and affective effects of voice-based technologies. We find that the use of DVA’s results in changes in the affective environments of the home, such as by creating uncertainty, harshness and intervening in cultural and temporal enactments of politeness. Moreover, their ability to make voices travel beyond the material confines of the home, renders its boundaries more permeable, thus creating a sense of disempowerment both towards technology and the management of the privacy of the home. We propose the phenomenon of voice and DVA’s in older people’s smart homes as an interesting topic for socio-gerontechnology research.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677329"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital Voice Assistants DVA","Eldercare Technology","Ethnographic study","Socio Gerontechnology","Sonic Affective Environments"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"then i just speak to it more harshly digital voice assistants and sonic affective infrastructures in older people s smart homes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-677329","ids":["itu-b16c52b5-2b57-4c4c-9f2f-7c3b10f3dc4b"],"keyword":["Digital Voice Assistants (DVA)","Eldercare Technology","Ethnographic Study","Socio-Gerontechnology","Sonic-Affective Environments"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B8526CAE6515ACD50CA582C503F4076"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Digital Societies and Participation Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b16c52b5-2b57-4c4c-9f2f-7c3b10f3dc4b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Then I just speak to it more harshly” : Digital voice assistants and sonic-affective infrastructures in older people’s smart homes","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677329","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Scholars of ageing and technology are becoming increasingly interested in how technology and ageing can be seen as mutually constitutive, an in­terest that is beginning to form new research agendas, alliances and fields of their own. Different concepts have been used to theorise and analyse this relationship of mutual construction. This article explores a concept from Science and technology studies, which has not previously been put in direct relation to ageing, namely the concept of infrastructure. It pro­poses the notion of “infrastructuring ageing” as a theoretical-analytical approach for studying the mutual constitution of ageing and technol­ogy. This approach implies slightly new versions of, or attentions to, the non-human actor, agency and socio-technical transformation, and opens up to fresh ethnographic views on the social, material and techno-political transformations of ageing.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382852"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","Gerotechnology","Infrastructuring","Non human agency","STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructuring ageing theorizing non human agency in ageing amp technology studies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ijal.1652-8670.3556","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382852","identifier":[{"id":"85129370177","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69b7cdb5-c1b2-47b1-b2f9-dd0a88587731"],"keyword":["STS","ageing","gerotechnology","infrastructuring","non-human agency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-94D0CACCA4A84F8375AB314454315FB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ijal.1652-8670.3556","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/ijal.1652-8670.3556","issn":["16528670"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal of Ageing and Later Life","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Ageing and Later Life","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129370177"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69b7cdb5-c1b2-47b1-b2f9-dd0a88587731"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructuring Ageing : Theorizing non-human agency in ageing &amp; technology studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382852","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we explore the form of care known as ‘active ageing’ by attending to its expression in care policies and within a Danish care home. We argue that active ageing policies gain their efficacy through reference to ‘the good life’, which is something the policies frame as ensuing if the elderly take on an active lifestyle. In the care home, the concept of active ageing gains its efficacy through its relation to other concepts of care, such as ‘lazy care’. The importance of the article lies in its demonstrating the dependence of policy concepts on other concepts (established or emerging), which lie in its shadow yet do important political work. Attending to shadow concepts is useful if trying to understand the inner mechanics of popular concepts in care policy, as well as the norms and resistance to which they give rise.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Winthereik, Brit Ross"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383246"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active ageing","Practice","care policy","politics of ageing","shadow concepts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"policy concepts and their shadows active ageing cold care lazy care and coffee talk care","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi.org/10.23987/sts.111019","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383246","identifier":[{"id":"85144791737","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-870f4657-520c-4d91-a3d2-3b5be39ad59e"],"keyword":["active ageing","care policy","politics of ageing","practice","shadow concepts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-46BEF043A0784DF8F976C217A9BE67DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi.org/10.23987/sts.111019","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://sciencetechnologystudies.journal.fi/article/view/111019/67133","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brit Ross","key":"winthereikpau","last":"Winthereik","name":"Winthereik, Brit Ross","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23987/sts.111019","issn":["22434690"],"journal":"Science & Technology Studies","publisher":"Finnish Society for Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"Science & Technology Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144791737"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-870f4657-520c-4d91-a3d2-3b5be39ad59e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Policy Concepts and Their Shadows : Active Ageing, Cold Care, Lazy Care and Coffee-Talk Care","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383246","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Social change in the twenty-first century is shaped by both demographic changes associated with ageing societies and significant technological change and development. Outlining the basic principles of a new academic field, Socio-gerontechnology, this book explores common conceptual, theoretical and methodological ideas that become visible in the critical scholarship on ageing and technology at the intersection of Age Studies and Science and Technology Studies (STS).","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Lassen, Aske Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384407"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socio gerontechnology interdisciplinary critical studies of ageing and technology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85105390338","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384407","identifier":[{"id":"85105390338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d5491450-527b-4bf3-87ea-4a38c3c74e08"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-4-5CEC8A2E20913B8E1BF330EF2293ADCE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aske Juul","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","name":"Lassen, Aske Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9780429278266","edition":"1st Edition","eisbn":["9780429278266"],"place":"London","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","subtitle":"Interdisciplinary Critical Studies of Ageing and Technology","title":"Socio-gerontechnology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105368540"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d5491450-527b-4bf3-87ea-4a38c3c74e08"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Socio-gerontechnology : Interdisciplinary Critical Studies of Ageing and Technology","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384407","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been celebrated as a breakthrough in eldercare. Mainstream discourses emphasize voice-based technology as practical assistants, and thus figure voice as a practical means to achieve certain ends. But there is more to voice interactions than merely distributing messages and articulating commands. Voice-based interactions create sonic environments, enact affect, identities, likes and dislikes. The paper explores the co-existence of older people and voice-based technologies ethnographically, and through the STS concept of infrastructure and a cultural anthropological view on voice. We see infrastructures as both objects and the relations between objects (Larkin), as ‘complex chains of material relations’ that ‘reconfigure bodies, societies [..] knowledge and discourses in ways often unnoticed’ (Harvey, Jensen and Morita). Voice is both a sonic material phenomenon and a culturally elaborated metaphor (Weidman), which connects deeply to feelings of intimacy, identity and community. Voice-based interactions can thus be seen as infrastructures that link the realms of the technical, cultural and sociopolitical to the level of the individual, creating sites where shared discourses and values, affect, and aesthetics are made manifest in and contested through embodied and material practice. With the increasing co-existence of older people and voice-based assistants, we see a need for ethnographic views on what these technologies are, how they can be studied, and what they do. We develop the notion of ‘infrastructures of voice and affect’ as a more-than-human approach to study entanglements of ageing, environments of affect and intimacy, and voice- based technology.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718859"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affect and intimacy","Ageing","Cultural anthropology","Eldercare","Ethnography","Infrastructures of voice","Material practices","Technocultural entanglements","Voice based interactions","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructures of voice environments of affect amp intimacy voice based technology and older people","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718859","ids":["itu-62b8ea0d-ab92-471a-ae9e-02c05cb1aa1a"],"keyword":["Affect and intimacy","Ageing","Cultural anthropology","Eldercare","Ethnography","Infrastructures of voice","Material practices","Technocultural entanglements","Voice-based interactions","Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C112D6973110624253D0A0B17232A5DD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-62b8ea0d-ab92-471a-ae9e-02c05cb1aa1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Infrastructures of Voice, Environments of Affect &amp; Intimacy:  : Voice-based Technology and Older People","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718859","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Voice-enabled technology has been seen as a breakthrough in eldercare, as practical assistants, and as social companions for older people. While dominant innovation discourses articulate these technologies as means to an end, research based on sociotechnical understandings has shown how technology, ageing and care cannot be seen as separate from each other, but as co-constituted (Peine et al., 2021). Building on this view, and through a focus on sociotechnical imaginaries we explore how voice-enabled technologies are slowly beginning to transform care, ageing and the home, as they are increasingly pervading public, political and corporate discourses, and put into use in the homes and everyday practices of older people. Sociotechnical imaginaries are, drawing on Jasanoff’s definition; “collectively held, publicly performed visions of desirable futures, animated by shared understandings of forms of social life, and social order attainable through, and supportive of, advances in science and technology” (Jasanoff 2015, 19). Sociotechnical imaginaries are at once descriptive of attainable futures and prescriptive of the kinds of futures that ought to be attained. This paper explores how sociotechnical imaginaries of voice-enabled technologies, ageing and care are being co-constituted in different sites through analyses of documents and visual representations, and ethnographic studies with older people using voice-enabled technologies. We look at big tech companies’ imaginaries of ageing and care vis a vis voice-enabled technologies, and explore how such imaginaries are being performed and negotiated in interactions between older people and voice-based technologies. The paper contributes to the philosophy of technology by giving empirical examples of how concrete voice-enabled technologies take part in forming sociotechnical imaginaries and futures of ageing, care and the home.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677310"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","Eldercare","Philosophy of technology","Sociotechnical imaginaries","Voice enabled technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voice enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care ageing and the home voice enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care ageing and the home","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.2021spt.com/abstracts/Book_of_abstracts_rl2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677310","ids":["itu-4bef3484-779b-41a2-b32b-9db20db9e659"],"keyword":["Ageing","Eldercare","Philosophy of technology","Sociotechnical imaginaries","Voice-enabled technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-61E3088AED515718EE2104AA68EEE11B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.2021spt.com/abstracts/Book_of_abstracts_rl2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4bef3484-779b-41a2-b32b-9db20db9e659"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voice-enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care, ageing and the home : Voice-enabled technologies and sociotechnical imaginaries of care, ageing and the home","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677310","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This chapter explores how Socio-gerontechnology can develop analyses that interfere with pervasive discourses on technology and ageing in ways that work against singularity and fixity. Inspired by recent debates in Science and Technology Studies about a turn to ontology, we analyse the emergence of prototypes in an innovation project seeking to develop digital solutions for older people. We analyse two prototypes, the Telenoid and the Tiles, through their appearance in different socio-material situations and inspired by the notion that apparently stabile things and realities can contain ‘shadowlands of alterity’. The analysis attends to alterity in different ways, by depicting the prototypes in ways that differ from dominating narratives about innovation and robotics and by showing how the prototypes ‘differed from themselves’ in the way that they were bound up with different political ontologies in different situations dependent on the circumstances in which they were made to emerge. We propose that the ontological debates present and enforce a mode of reflexivity that may enable Socio-gerontechnology studies to engage with their subject matters in new ways in order to avoid and interfere with reified and potentially stereotypical ideas about ageing, technology and innovation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Lassen, Aske Juul"],"cuid":["S02-090.54-038293"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fragile robots and coincidental innovation turning socio gerontechnology towards ontology","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780429278266-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.54-038293","identifier":[{"id":"85105388790","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4400c5e3-0be8-453f-a282-0a9c6a8b1a6d","ku-1fc84b76-2afd-4821-b456-bb13331ba5a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-137D6E1D0A74D361CFDE4E07645C97D5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/49553","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780429278266-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/299877765/10.4324_9780429278266_4_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aske Juul","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"e814e4bf-28f9-4f8c-924f-243af3588856","name":"Lassen, Aske Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexander","key":"peinepedh","last":"Peine","name":"Peine, Alexander","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara","key":"lmarshallpedh","last":"L. Marshall","name":"L. Marshall, Barbara","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara L.","key":"marshallpedh","last":"Marshall","name":"Marshall, Barbara L.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Wendy","key":"martinpedh","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Wendy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Louis","key":"nevenpedh","last":"Neven","name":"Neven, Louis","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9780429278266-4","eisbn":["9780429278266"],"isbn":["9780367230821"],"publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","subtitle":"Interdisciplinary Critical Studies of Ageing and Technology","title":"Socio-gerontechnology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105388790"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4400c5e3-0be8-453f-a282-0a9c6a8b1a6d","ku-1fc84b76-2afd-4821-b456-bb13331ba5a1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fragile Robots and Coincidental Innovation : Turning Socio-Gerontechnology towards Ontology","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.54-038293","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382255"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fragile robots and coincidental innovation turning socio gerontechnology towards ontology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382255","ids":["itu-4284ee5a-fc24-412e-8ffe-f44963b4b12c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F0A162EABB74E6D9BEFB5F1E9F616C7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4284ee5a-fc24-412e-8ffe-f44963b4b12c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fragile Robots and Coincidental Innovation : Turning Socio-Gerontechnology towards Ontology","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382255","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"New technologies are implemented in health care with the promises of replacing care work, but implementing technology into care also requires a lot of work. On the basis of ethnographic fieldwork in a Danish homecare unit, this paper explores a phenomenon increasingly pervading the work of health care personnel in the Nordic countries and other welfare states around the world; the implementation of technology in health and elder care. The paper asks what work is involved in making new technologies enter health and elder care. Drawing on STS research on technology implementation, the paper analyses the invisible work of technology implementation, a complex process that involves skilled affective, symbolic, and evocative practices such as enchanting, affecting, and evoking certain imaginaries and beliefs. What is being implemented along these processes, the paper argues is not only technology, but also new municipal and home care workers reconfigured as ‘implementation agents’, and ‘digital older citizens","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382614"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Health Working Environment Wellbeing Innovation Productivity Gender Ethnicity Age and Diversity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enchanting evoking and affecting the invisible work of technology implementation in homecare","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18291/njwls.v9iS5.112690","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382614","identifier":[{"id":"85073772454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5ab3596e-12a8-4650-bb50-d75a791d4b16"],"keyword":["Health, Working Environment & Wellbeing, Innovation & Productivity, Gender, Ethnicity, Age and Diversity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F2FB45A440BFC5F9626FB7B3996ECDCC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84417024/Enchanting_Evoking_and_Affecting.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/njwls/article/view/112690/161429","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18291/njwls.v9iS5.112690","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18291/njwls.v9is5.112690","issn":["22450157"],"issue":"S5","journal":"Nordic Journal of Working Life Studies","pages":"33-47","paperid":"S5","publisher":"Roskilde University","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Working Life Studies","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073772454"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5ab3596e-12a8-4650-bb50-d75a791d4b16"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enchanting, Evoking, and Affecting : The Invisible Work of Technology Implementation in Homecare","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382614","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Time is a matter of great concern to healthcare and eldercare. In situations of austerity, time is both an essential resource and an issue – what to spend time on? how to save time? Care and innovation both consume time, but they are also practices that generate (or assemble) time in different ways. This paper explores the different ways of assembling ageing, time, technology and care in differently located practices; a Danish innovation project aiming at developing technologies for older people, and a Danish home care unit seeking to implement new technologies of care. Drawing on empirical observations of the controversies emerging around time and technology, we inquire into the ontology of time. Performative approaches to care and innovation have asked questions about the socio-material nature of things like technology, bodies, disease and care. In this paper we engage with the materiality of time, and ask how different material practices perform time in different ways. Based on ethnographic observations of controversies around time in practices of eldercare and innovation we ask what kind of a thing is time? Technologies for care-work promise to save and recover time, but, we contend, they also change what time is, which creates controversies when implemented in practice where other types of time prevail.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Yndigegn, Signe Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382606"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ageing","CARE","Innovation","Technology","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"matters of time the different times of technological innovation and care practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382606","ids":["itu-5a453ef8-163c-413e-acc0-6fa6df15f09c"],"keyword":["Ageing","Care","Innovation","Time","technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80A37543C14AB3DA8BE396F98D580176"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Louise","key":"yndigegnpau","last":"Yndigegn","locid":"b3e022c2-a124-41f0-a7fc-4c4f6ab5e99c","name":"Yndigegn, Signe Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-3438-7288","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5a453ef8-163c-413e-acc0-6fa6df15f09c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Matters of time : the different times of technological innovation and care practice.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382606","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The fact that the average citizen in Western societies is aging has significant implications for national welfare models. What some call ’the grey tsunami’ has resulted in suggestions for, and experiments in, re-designing healthcare systems and elderly care. In Denmark, one attempted solution to these challenges has been the development of welfare technologies and services. A range of projects is currently being initiated, all with the shared aim to create technological and social innovations for health care and elderly care. This PhD thesis focuses on practices of developing welfare technologies within one such project, Project Lev Vel, a public-private and user driven innovation project. The central questions posed by the dissertation are: What is welfare technology? How is it imagined, designed, and developed, and by whom? Who are driving the design processes and how? Who are the elderly users that are imagined as the target group for welfare technology, and where are they located? Based on ethnographic explorations of ’welfare technology’ and related figures that include not only ’the elderly’, but also ’prototypes’ and ’partnership’ the dissertation analyses the processes and socio-technical arrangements through which welfare technology, as concept and practice, emerges. Despite high expectations for the positive effects of welfare technology in Danish government policies, the practical development of technological solutions turned out to be a difficult task. What caused such difficulties? The dissertation aims to elucidate the activities of design, and the development of welfare technology within the framework of public-private (PPI) and user driven innovation (UDI) project. One of the main findings is that for design carried out under the auspices of PPI and UDI, the crafting of sociotechnical sites and infrastructures for project communication plays a central role for design and, ultimately, for what welfare technology comes to be. The chapters explore different processes of what I call infrastructuring design; the ongoing crafting of social, material, and technical arrangements for collaborative design to happen. The implication of this is that technological design should not be imagined as the foundation for shaping more effective health care practices and better welfare. Instead, possibilities for improving practices through welfare technology emerge out of heterogeneous assemblages, in which not only technologies but also other materialities and diverse subjectivities all play important roles. Presently, relatively little is known about the co-emergence of welfare technology and design practice. The perspective of this thesis opens up for novel ways of exploring the ’social life’ of innovative welfare technologies. In general, the thesis offers an alternative to conventional views that depict design as driven, as if naturally, by its methods (a view that might be called ’methods fetishism’), and as leading, again, as if naturally, to the development of ’better’ technologies (a view that might be called teleological design). Instead of such reified views, the dissertation offers an account of design practices that takes seriously the continuous negotiations among heterogeneous actors out of which welfare technologies may emerge, or not.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S02-086.49-038262"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infrastructuring design an ethnographic study of welfare technologies and design in a public private and user driven innovation project","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109064500/INFRASTRUCTURING_DESIGN_print_version_FINAL_feb_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.49-038262","ids":["itu-19f65a92-6bf6-4f4c-9806-d47033712585","ku-79b97de1-ecd1-40f7-8dd6-ece67cd8fb50"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-A3D57300DF0C593D42C70ED43E38CC43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.forskningsdatabasen.dk/en/catalog/2292259641","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109064500/INFRASTRUCTURING_DESIGN_print_version_FINAL_feb_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History, Copenhagen Centre for Health Research in the Humanities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"3afe4f0a-b4c7-4be1-bd13-57910c9b9cfb","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779493353"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"116","pages":"252","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-19f65a92-6bf6-4f4c-9806-d47033712585","ku-79b97de1-ecd1-40f7-8dd6-ece67cd8fb50"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"INFRASTRUCTURING DESIGN : An Ethnographic Study of Welfare Technologies and Design in a Public-Private and User Driven Innovation Project","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.49-038262","year":2016,"yearsub":2016}
{"abstract":"This article explores problems of representing the elderly in a User Driven Innovation (UDI) project developing welfare technology. Drawing on Helen Verran’s concept of the dual logics of generalization I attend to differences in enactments of the elderly. I engage with situations where the objects we study do not seem to ‘fit’ with the categories available or when they seem ‘more than one, but less than many’, and I relate these issues to two different logics of generalization. The contribution of the paper to design studies, and designers who experience difficulties inscribing the elderly into design, is that it shows how Science and Technology Studies (STS) can be useful in order to better recognize differences between different enactments of an imagined user, in this case the elderly. The contribution of the paper to STS is a discussion of how I as an STS-informed ethnographer was invited to participate in a user driven innovation project. Based on my reflections on this role, the paper reflects on the ethnographic account as a tool with particular qualities and limitations when inhabiting a position as mediator between users and an innovation project.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383078"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Elderly Representation","Ethnographic Mediation","Science and Technology Studies STS","User Driven Innovation UDI","Welfare technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"different generalizations of the elderly indesign of welfare technology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.dasts.dk/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Marie-Ertner-2016-Different-generalizations-.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383078","ids":["itu-7b567976-4512-4f84-9093-fecf64de9042"],"keyword":["Elderly Representation","Ethnographic Mediation","Science and Technology Studies (STS)","User Driven Innovation (UDI)","Welfare Technology"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1DA80736A13D88EA3A8EC9FCB7D9D9AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.dasts.dk/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Marie-Ertner-2016-Different-generalizations-.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"0cc78e11-da3d-4687-a49a-76a2ba39c292","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19044372"],"issue":"1","journal":"STS Encounters","pages":"1-28","paperid":"1","publisher":"Danish Association for Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"STS Encounters","title_org":"STS Encounters - DASTS working paper series","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7b567976-4512-4f84-9093-fecf64de9042"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Different generalizations of the elderly indesign of welfare technology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383078","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"welfare technologies are often seen as solutions to problems related to ageing and elderly care. A PhD study of welfare technologies for so-called active elderly people shows another reality of what welfare technologies are and do.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425064"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvem bestemmer hvad en gangstav skal bruges til et etnografisk studie af velfærdsteknologier og deres brugere","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-425064","ids":["ku-353da0db-600e-440a-8692-20589137f808"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D59E05557EEF0AEA59C29F113EE298B4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History, Copenhagen Centre for Health Research in the Humanities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"3afe4f0a-b4c7-4be1-bd13-57910c9b9cfb","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16048644"],"journal":"Gerontologi","pages":"8-11","status":"p","title":"Gerontologi","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-353da0db-600e-440a-8692-20589137f808"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hvem bestemmer, hvad en gangstav skal bruges til? : Et etnografisk studie af velfærdsteknologier og deres brugere","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425064","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Ertner, Sara Marie","Lassen, Aske Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412662"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-30","place":"Nice, fr","start":"2016-09-28","title":"The 10th World Conference of Gerontechnology","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Humanities","Gerontologi"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconfiguring old age through rehabilitation technologies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-412662","ids":["ku-2040211c-7b8e-4383-881d-bfe2c365bd35"],"keyword":["Faculty of Humanities","Gerontologi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D2A66FB4A20FC2C17F36677FFC9E3BAF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, SAXO-Institute - Archaeology, Ethnology, Greek & Latin, History, Copenhagen Centre for Health Research in the Humanities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara Marie","key":"ertnerpau","last":"Ertner","locid":"3afe4f0a-b4c7-4be1-bd13-57910c9b9cfb","name":"Ertner, Sara Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Aske Juul","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"e814e4bf-28f9-4f8c-924f-243af3588856","name":"Lassen, Aske Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish